1.1 Navigation Architecture Overview

The V3 sidebar is a transparent, merged navigation rail living inside the single main glass container. It is not a separate panel — it shares the #05060A base with a backdrop-filter: blur(32px) saturate(140%) glass treatment inherited from the parent shell. The nav is separated from the content area by a broken/interrupted vertical divider — never a solid line.

Structural rules:

Nav width: 68px collapsed (icon-only), 240px expanded
Collapsed is default on load; hover or pin expands
Expansion uses the V3 transition: 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) on width + opacity for labels
The broken vertical divider is 1px wide, uses repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(255,255,255,0.33) 0px, rgba(255,255,255,0.33) 12px, transparent 12px, transparent 20px)
Active nav item: background: rgba(255,255,255,0.06), border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12), border-radius: 10px
Hover (non-active): background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03), no border
Icons: 20px Lucide, color rgba(255,255,255,0.45) default, rgba(255,255,255,0.95) active
Submenu items indent 16px from parent, appear with 0.3s fade+slideDown on parent click
Submenus visible only when sidebar is expanded
