2.3 Glass Treatment & The 77.7% Main Card Contract
2.3.1 The Main Card

The entire application lives inside a single glass container that occupies exactly 77.7% of the viewport (centered, with the base gradient visible as a thin frame around all edges).

.v3-main-card {
  position: fixed;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  width: 77.7%;
  height: 77.7%;
  min-width: 1200px;
  min-height: 700px;
  max-width: 1800px;
  max-height: 1000px;

  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
  backdrop-filter: blur(32px) saturate(140%);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(32px) saturate(140%);

  border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.33);
  border-radius: 20px;

  overflow: hidden;
  display: flex;
}

2.3.2 Why 77.7%

The 77.7% ratio creates a visible dark frame around the app — like a premium device bezel. This frame:

Shows the --v3-bg-gradient void beneath
Creates psychological "breathing room"
Makes the glass container feel like a physical object floating in space
Differentiates V3 from typical edge-to-edge SaaS layouts
