2.7 The Multipage Transition System

This is the most critical motion system in V3. Every view change — nav click, tab switch, drawer open, route change — must feel like pages of a premium physical portfolio being turned.

2.7.1 Core Transition Specification
Property	Value
Duration	0.6s (primary), 0.8s (complex/full-page)
Easing	cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) — "V3 ease" (fast start, luxurious settle)
Properties animated	opacity, transform, filter
Never animate	background-color, border-color (these use 120ms ease for micro-interactions)
2.7.2 Page Transition (Route Change)

When navigating between top-level routes (e.g., Dashboard → Clinician Profiles):

Outgoing page:

.v3-page-exit {
  animation: v3PageOut 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) forwards;
}
@keyframes v3PageOut {
  0%   { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1) translateY(0); filter: blur(0); }
  100% { opacity: 0; transform: scale(0.98) translateY(-8px); filter: blur(4px); }
}


Incoming page:

.v3-page-enter {
  animation: v3PageIn 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) forwards;
}
@keyframes v3PageIn {
  0%   { opacity: 0; transform: scale(0.98) translateY(12px); filter: blur(6px); }
  100% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1) translateY(0); filter: blur(0); }
}


Implementation with Framer Motion:

// src/components/shell/PageTransition.tsx
import { motion, AnimatePresence } from 'framer-motion';
import { useLocation } from 'react-router-dom';
const V3_EASE = [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1];
const pageVariants = {
initial: {
opacity: 0,
scale: 0.98,
y: 12,
filter: 'blur(6px)',
},
enter: {
opacity: 1,
scale: 1,
y: 0,
filter: 'blur(0px)',
transition: { duration: 0.6, ease: V3_EASE },
},
exit: {
opacity: 0,
scale: 0.98,
y: -8,
filter: 'blur(4px)',
transition: { duration: 0.4, ease: V3_EASE },
},
};
export function PageTransition({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
const location = useLocation();
return (
<AnimatePresence mode="wait">
<motion.div
key={location.pathname}
variants={pageVariants}
initial="initial"
animate="enter"
exit="exit"
style={{ width: '100%', height: '100%' }}
>
{children}
</motion.div>
</AnimatePresence>
);
}
2.7.3 Tab Switch Transition

When switching tabs within a page (e.g., HR Policies → Compliance → Training):

const tabVariants = {
  initial: { opacity: 0, x: 16, filter: 'blur(4px)' },
  enter: {
    opacity: 1, x: 0, filter: 'blur(0px)',
    transition: { duration: 0.4, ease: V3_EASE },
  },
  exit: {
    opacity: 0, x: -16, filter: 'blur(4px)',
    transition: { duration: 0.25, ease: V3_EASE },
  },
};


Direction-aware: if switching to a tab on the right, enter from right (x: 16), exit left (x: -16). If switching left, reverse.

