2.10 Polish & Consistency Rules

No shadows. The entire system uses border + backdrop-filter for depth. Box-shadow is banned except for focus rings (0 0 0 2px rgba(0,121,112,0.4)).

No gradients on surfaces. Gradients exist only on: (a) the body background, (b) the logo element, (c) the broken line separator. Everything else is flat.

No colored backgrounds for sections. Kanban columns use 4% accent tint — that's the maximum color saturation allowed on any background.

Borders are structural, not decorative. Every border must serve a purpose (containment, separation, hierarchy). If removing a border doesn't reduce clarity, remove it.

Whitespace is a design element. Minimum padding inside any container: 12px. Minimum gap between cards in a grid: 12px. Main content area padding: 24px 32px.

Text never touches edges. Minimum 8px clearance between text and its container border.

Scrollbars are always hidden. Use CSS scroll-hiding on all scrollable containers.

The broken line separator is the only decorative structural element allowed. It replaces solid dividers everywhere in the nav.

Hover states are mandatory on all interactive elements. No element should feel "dead" when hovered.

Loading states use skeleton screens — not spinners. Skeletons use rgba(255,255,255,0.04) with a shimmer animation at rgba(255,255,255,0.06).

